IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp5-months`
IMPORT `cp5-d-child`
IMPORT `cp5-d-post-retirement`

-- Tests of sections 74 to 76.2 (cp5-d-child.l4 and cp5-d-post-retirement.l4). Expected values were worked out by hand
-- from the text (and from regulation 65.1(b) for "maintaining the child").

§ `Tests of sections 74 to 76.2`

§§ `Subsection 74(1)`

#ASSERT `s 74(1) — the application may be made on behalf of the disabled contributor's child or orphan by the applicant` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74(1) — the application may be made on behalf of the disabled contributor's child or orphan by the applicant` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 74(1) — the application may be made on behalf of the disabled contributor's child or orphan by the applicant` FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Subsection 74(2)(a) -- a disabled contributor's child's benefit`

-- The twelfth month before the month following the month of an application on 5 September 2020 is October 2019.
#ASSERT `s 74(2) — the earliest month for which a benefit is payable, by reason of the application` (YearMonthDay 2020 9 5) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 10 1
-- Across a year end: an application in March 2021 reaches back to April 2020.
#ASSERT `s 74(2) — the earliest month for which a benefit is payable, by reason of the application` (YearMonthDay 2021 3 31) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 4 1
-- The contributor's disability pension is first payable for August 2020; the child was born 12 January 2019 (February 2019 next follows): August 2020.
#ASSERT `s 74(2)(a) — the first month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2019 1 12) (YearMonthDay 2020 9 5) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 8 1)
-- The child became a child of the contributor on 20 October 2020: the month next following, November 2020.
#ASSERT `s 74(2)(a) — the first month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 10 20) (YearMonthDay 2020 11 5) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 11 1)
-- Application on 5 September 2022: not earlier than October 2021.
#ASSERT `s 74(2)(a) — the first month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2019 1 12) (YearMonthDay 2022 9 5) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 10 1)
-- Not approved.
#ASSERT `s 74(2)(a) — the first month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2019 1 12) (YearMonthDay 2020 9 5) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Subsection 74(2)(b) -- an orphan's benefit`

-- The contributor died 10 March 2021: April 2021; the child was born 2 February 2010: March 2010; application 1 May 2021.
#ASSERT `s 74(2)(b) — the first month for which an orphan's benefit is payable` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 2 2) (YearMonthDay 2021 5 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1)
-- A child born after the death (15 June 2021): the month next following the birth, July 2021.
#ASSERT `s 74(2)(b) — the first month for which an orphan's benefit is payable` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2021 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2021 8 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 7 1)
-- Application on 1 March 2023: not earlier than April 2022.
#ASSERT `s 74(2)(b) — the first month for which an orphan's benefit is payable` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 2 2) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 4 1)
#ASSERT `s 74(2)(b) — the first month for which an orphan's benefit is payable` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2021 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 2 2) (YearMonthDay 2021 5 1) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Subsections 74(3) and (3.1)`

-- A benefit already payable in respect of another contributor, who is not a parent of the person: barred.
#ASSERT `s 74(3) — the benefit is not payable to the person in respect of the contributor` TRUE FALSE 1
-- ... but another parent of the person: allowed (the second contributor).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 74(3) — the benefit is not payable to the person in respect of the contributor` TRUE TRUE 1)
-- ... but never for more than two contributors.
#ASSERT `s 74(3) — the benefit is not payable to the person in respect of the contributor` TRUE TRUE 2
-- No benefit yet: not barred.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 74(3) — the benefit is not payable to the person in respect of the contributor` FALSE FALSE 0)
#ASSERT `s 74(3.1) — the person is a parent of the child` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 74(3.1) — the person is a parent of the child` FALSE)

§§ `Section 75`

-- A child born 15 June 2010 is not treated as reaching 18 until 1 July 2028.
#ASSERT `s 75(1) — to whom a disabled contributor's child's benefit or orphan's benefit is paid` (YearMonthDay 2010 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30) TRUE EQUALS JUST `the benefit is paid to the person or agency having decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan`
#ASSERT `s 75(1) — to whom a disabled contributor's child's benefit or orphan's benefit is paid` (YearMonthDay 2010 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30) FALSE EQUALS JUST `the benefit is paid to the person or agency the Minister directs`
#ASSERT `s 75(1) — to whom a disabled contributor's child's benefit or orphan's benefit is paid` (YearMonthDay 2010 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2028 6 30) TRUE EQUALS JUST `the benefit is paid to the person or agency having decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan`
-- On 1 July 2028 the child has reached 18: the subsection says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 75(1) — to whom a disabled contributor's child's benefit or orphan's benefit is paid` (YearMonthDay 2010 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2028 7 1) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Subsection (2): the presumption.
#ASSERT `s 75(2) — the person presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan` FALSE FALSE FALSE 60 EQUALS `the contributor is presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child`
-- Exactly 20% of the parenting time is not "less than 20%".
#ASSERT `s 75(2) — the person presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan` FALSE FALSE FALSE 20 EQUALS `the contributor is presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child`
#ASSERT `s 75(2) — the person presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan` FALSE FALSE FALSE 19.99 EQUALS `no one is presumed to have decision-making responsibility under subsection 75(2)`
-- Evidence to the contrary.
#ASSERT `s 75(2) — the person presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan` FALSE TRUE FALSE 60 EQUALS `no one is presumed to have decision-making responsibility under subsection 75(2)`
-- An orphan: the survivor, if any, with 20% or more.
#ASSERT `s 75(2) — the person presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan` TRUE FALSE TRUE 50 EQUALS `the survivor of the contributor is presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the orphan`
#ASSERT `s 75(2) — the person presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan` TRUE FALSE TRUE 19 EQUALS `no one is presumed to have decision-making responsibility under subsection 75(2)`
#ASSERT `s 75(2) — the person presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan` TRUE FALSE FALSE 50 EQUALS `no one is presumed to have decision-making responsibility under subsection 75(2)`

§§ `Section 76`

-- Regulation 65.1(b): periodic provision of not less than the benefit ($350).
#ASSERT `s 76(1)(d) — the disabled contributor is maintaining the child, as defined by regulation 65.1(b)` TRUE 400 350
#ASSERT `s 76(1)(d) — the disabled contributor is maintaining the child, as defined by regulation 65.1(b)` TRUE 350 350
#ASSERT NOT (`s 76(1)(d) — the disabled contributor is maintaining the child, as defined by regulation 65.1(b)` TRUE 349.99 350)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 76(1)(d) — the disabled contributor is maintaining the child, as defined by regulation 65.1(b)` FALSE 400 350)
-- (a) ceased to be a dependent child in December 2025; (b) died January 2026: the earlier, December 2025.
#ASSERT `s 76(1) — the last month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 3)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 9)) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1)
-- (b) alone.
#ASSERT `s 76(1) — the last month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 9)) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1)
-- (c) the contributor's disability pension ceased in March 2025.
#ASSERT `s 76(1) — the last month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 3)) NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 3 31)) NOTHING FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1)
-- (d) adopted by a stranger in June 2025, the contributor not maintaining the child.
#ASSERT `s 76(1) — the last month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 3)) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 6 14)) FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1)
-- (d) the contributor is maintaining the child: the adoption does not end the benefit.
#ASSERT `s 76(1) — the last month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 3)) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 6 14)) TRUE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1)
-- (e) the contributor ceased to have parenting time in February 2025, and the child is a child by reason of it.
#ASSERT `s 76(1) — the last month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 3)) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 2 20)) TRUE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 2 1)
-- (e) the child is a child on another ground: the loss of parenting time does not end the benefit.
#ASSERT `s 76(1) — the last month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 3)) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 2 20)) FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1)
-- No event: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 76(1) — the last month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Orphan's benefit.
#ASSERT `s 76(2) — the last month for which an orphan's benefit is payable` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 6 30)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 1 9)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 6 1)
#ASSERT `s 76(2) — the last month for which an orphan's benefit is payable` NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 1 9)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 76(2) — the last month for which an orphan's benefit is payable` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Subsection (3): born 10 March 2000, 18 reached 1 April 2018, before the contributor's death on 15 February 2019.
#ASSERT `s 76(3) — the month in which an application for an orphan's benefit is deemed made by the person` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2000 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2019 2 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2019 2 1)
-- Born 10 March 2001: 18 is not reached (under section 2(2)) until 1 April 2019.
#ASSERT `s 76(3) — the month in which an application for an orphan's benefit is deemed made by the person` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2001 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2019 2 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76(3) — the month in which an application for an orphan's benefit is deemed made by the person` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2001 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2019 4 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2019 4 1)
#ASSERT `s 76(3) — the month in which an application for an orphan's benefit is deemed made by the person` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2019 2 15) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Sections 76.1 and 76.2`

-- Earnings of $10,000 in 2024 (exemption $3,500), retirement pension first payable March 2023, born 15 June 1960: January 2025.
#ASSERT `s 76.1 — the first month for which a post-retirement benefit is payable` TRUE TRUE 10000 3500 (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) 2024 EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1)
-- Earnings equal to the basic exemption do not exceed it.
#ASSERT `s 76.1 — the first month for which a post-retirement benefit is payable` TRUE TRUE 3500 3500 (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) 2024 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76.1 — the first month for which a post-retirement benefit is payable` TRUE TRUE 3500.01 3500 (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) 2024 EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1)
-- Not a beneficiary of a retirement pension; no contribution made.
#ASSERT `s 76.1 — the first month for which a post-retirement benefit is payable` FALSE TRUE 10000 3500 (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) 2024 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76.1 — the first month for which a post-retirement benefit is payable` TRUE FALSE 10000 3500 (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) 2024 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The period begins before the retirement pension commences (December 2022 for a pension first payable March 2023).
#ASSERT `s 76.1 — the first month for which a post-retirement benefit is payable` TRUE TRUE 10000 3500 (YearMonthDay 2022 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2024 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) 2024 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The period must begin after 2011: 2011-12-31 is not after 2011, 2012-01-01 is.
#ASSERT `s 76.1 — the first month for which a post-retirement benefit is payable` TRUE TRUE 10000 3500 (YearMonthDay 2011 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2012 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2011 12 1) (YearMonthDay 1950 6 15) 2012 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76.1 — the first month for which a post-retirement benefit is payable` TRUE TRUE 10000 3500 (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2012 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1950 6 15) 2012 EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 1 1)
-- The period must end with the month before the month of reaching 70 (July 2030 for a person born 15 June 1960).
#ASSERT `s 76.1 — the first month for which a post-retirement benefit is payable` TRUE TRUE 10000 3500 (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2030 6 30) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) 2030 EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2031 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 76.1 — the first month for which a post-retirement benefit is payable` TRUE TRUE 10000 3500 (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2030 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) 2030 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 76.2.
#ASSERT `s 76.2 — the last month for which a post-retirement benefit is paid` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 8 1)
#ASSERT `s 76.2 — the last month for which a post-retirement benefit is paid` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
